{%- comment -%}
  The Markdown twin of a glossary term, /hub/glossary/<term>.md (src/frontend/src/pages/hub/[...page].md.ts): type,
  pronunciation, description, aliases, the body (`content`, the term's Markdown after Liquid), the practical
  example, the learn-more links and the related terms in glossary order. It is the `content` template of a fork of
  the term pages (douze.yml: a `glossary-twins` fork step over hub/glossary/*/index.md, which the generic `twins`
  fork leaves out); it renders without HTML encoding. Reads the term's data, collections.glossary and `content`.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- include "partials/hub/glossary-terms" -%}
# {{ title }}
{% if termType %}
Term type: {{ termType }}
{% endif %}{% if pronunciation %}
Pronounced: {{ pronunciation }}
{% endif %}
{{ description }}
{% if aliases.size > 0 %}
Also known as: {{ aliases | join: ", " }}
{% endif %}
{{ content | strip }}

## Practical example

{{ context }}
{% if resources.size > 0 %}
## Learn more
{% for gtm_link in resources %}
- [{{ gtm_link.title }}](https://aspire.dev{{ gtm_link.href }})
{% endfor %}{% endif %}
## Related terms
{% for gtm_url in gt_urls %}{% assign gtm_id = gtm_url | remove_first: "/hub/glossary/" | remove: "/" %}{% if related contains gtm_id %}
- [{{ collections.urls[gtm_url].data.title }}](https://aspire.dev{{ gtm_url }})
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
